      "where": null,
      "problem": "Ezekiel 19:1 says the lament is for the princes of Israel, but the walkthrough never ties the mother, the young lions or the vine to Israel or its princes. It also never says who they stand for historically. For example, 2 Kings 23:31-34 tells of a king of Judah taken to Egypt. Without that, the baker may finish Prep without understanding what the lament is about.",
      "question": "In a prophetic lament, should Prep tie the images to the princes named in the passage, or to historical kings from other passages (with references)? Or should Prep leave the meaning of the images open because the text doesn't spell it out?",
